+// FILE: GXWorldStream.cpp ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+// GeneralsX @feature ZeroHourEarth 13/11/2026 World Exploration: the streaming window.
+// The design is in GameClient/GXWorldStream.h; the wire format is worldserver/server.py's.
+//
+// THREADS. One network thread only RECEIVES: it reads a frame, inflates a chunk if it is one, and
+// queues the message. Everything else - sending, parsing, every touch of the game - happens on the
+// game thread, in pump(). A game frame never waits for the network.
+//
+// COORDINATES. The world server speaks in chunks (cx, cy) of a grid anchored near where the session
+// was opened. The window's south-west chunk is (m_winCx, m_winCy); a chunk's corner in the game is
+// ((cx - m_winCx) * n * 10, (cy - m_winCy) * n * 10). When the window moves by a chunk, m_winCx
+// changes and everything in the game is moved the other way by n * 10 units (shiftWorld).
+//
+// THE CENTRE. What keeps the window where it is: the point the camera looks at (RTS / free camera,
+// the default), or the test vehicle while the camera follows it. Leaving the middle chunk by more
+// than a tenth of a chunk shifts the window one chunk that way.
+//
+// PRELOAD. The window plus kPrefetchRing chunks around it is kept downloaded (the server also reads ahead
+// in the direction of travel), and a chunk is parsed and its roads prepared on the network thread when it
+// arrives: a shift only places what is ready. What a shift still costs in the game thread is the ground
+// itself, the pathfinder (its terrain classes are cached and moved, only the strip is classified again) and
+// the radar picture.
+//
+// ROADS. Every chunk brings its road ribbons, reduced on arrival (prepareChunkLines). The window's roads
+// are rebuilt whole into the terrain's road buffer (W3DRoadBuffer::loadStreamRoads) at the start and after
+// late chunks (at most four times a second); a shift moves the drawn roads at once and rebuilds them a
+// moment later. The buffer links pieces only where their points are exactly equal.
+//
+// BRIDGES. A road the map data calls a bridge comes as a Roads.ini bridge with its deck height; its pieces
+// are joined across chunk edges, cut into straight spans and built as real game bridges (rebuildBridges).
+//
+// RADAR AND HORIZON. The minimap is drawn enlarged and centred on the camera (Radar::setStreamView), so it
+// scrolls instead of jumping a chunk; past the window the sky shows a distant land in the window's colours.
+///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+
